## How the slice was produced

From the images of commit `aaaabbbb`, one per `# image` row of `tools/cts/mali-gles2-tree.txt`, built with `tools/cts/imx95-deqp-images.sh`. Each image was staged as a file on the module's eMMC root file system (or its FAT boot-files partition), loaded at the module's own U-Boot prompt (`ext4load` or `fatload` to `0xd0000000`, md5 compared with the host's) and entered with `dcache off; icache flush; go 0xd0000000`; the rows were read on the UART_3 console, and the board came back by itself (PSCI reset or the watchdog). The boot partitions and the boot command were not written (`tools/cts/README.md` section 5). The slice holds no host name, address, user name, MAC address or serial; the raw console captures stay out of git.
